WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
- And many of your roles
that you played a mother,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.840
do you embrace that?

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.673
- Ah, yes.

00:00:04.673 --> 00:00:07.200
You know, it, the beginning of my career,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.900
I played everybody's mom.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.390
Jennifer Lewis always says
she's the mother of Hollywood,

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.749
but all of my children are famous now.

00:00:14.749 --> 00:00:16.817
(Audience laughing)

00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:17.650
- All are famous.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:21.750
- Viola Davis, Taraji
P. Henson, Regina Hall,

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.040
Regina King, Idris Elba.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.540
I mean, I could just go on and on.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.028
I played everybody's mom.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.150
- I think it was your magical influence.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:31.593
- Wow, wow, I mean I
just could go on and on.

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:33.070
It's so great, yes.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.370
- Well, my daughter is a fan.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.893
So you worked with Whitney
on Waiting to Exhale.

00:00:36.893 --> 00:00:37.726
- Yeah.

00:00:37.726 --> 00:00:39.280
- Oh, I loved it so much.

00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:43.500
What do you remember about that shoot,

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.620
like because I only have one
Whitney memory and it was like,

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.510
we were both at this
party and we got to be

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:48.343
in a picture together.

00:00:48.343 --> 00:00:51.030
And it's my favorite picture
in all of the worlds.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.070
It felt like cause, and we
didn't even really talk,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.100
but just her presence. I was so excited.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.310
Like I was so inspired by her.
So, what was your experience?

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.800
- She's so down to
earth and real and warm.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.870
And when we were doing Waiting to Exhale,

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.080
she would never stop singing.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.600
She was always singing in
the break, in the middle.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.541
I mean, as soon as he would say cut.

00:01:07.541 --> 00:01:08.374
- She was like,

00:01:08.374 --> 00:01:11.270
(Singing)

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.630
- My gosh.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.940
- And so, I just was
absolutely, loved her.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.480
She was just a joy to work with.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.080
I did three projects with
her, Waiting to Exhale,

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:21.200
Preacher's Wife.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.420
- I loved that one.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.740
- And the television show that
she got a chance to come on.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.700
So she was just a dream to work with.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.370
- Those two soundtracks
though, Waiting to Exhale,

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:30.040
Preacher's wife. What?

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.300
Oh my God.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.300
It's so funny that you said

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.640
she was singing all the time too,

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.960
because the one time I was
around her, she and Jamie Fox,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.180
they were just dancing the whole time.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.030
Like in the photo they're
dancing. No one else is dancing.

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.060
We're all standing there. We're like,

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.970
let her do what she wants
to do. Like It was like,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.370
it was like amazing. Anyway,

